.TH VAC 8 "2026-05-30" "versatile-autoreg-vac" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
vac \- Versatile Autoregistration Client daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vac
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vac
is a systemd service that automatically registers the local machine in a
.BR vas (8)
server and keeps a local copy of the network inventory.
.PP
On startup,
.B vac
waits for
.B VAS_HOST
to be defined, performs a blocking initial registration, then enters a
polling loop driven by two independent timers:
.TP
.B CHECK_SECONDS
Runs a local self-check (hostname, IP, MAC, extra fields) comparing
current values against
.IR /var/lib/vac/identity.json .
If anything has changed the client sends
.BR "POST /register" ;
otherwise it sends
.BR "POST /heartbeat" .
After the self-check, the local version is compared with
.BR "GET /version" ;
if a new version is available the inventory is downloaded and
.I identity.json
is refreshed from
.BR "GET /clients/{uuid}" .
.TP
.B HEARTBEAT_SECONDS
Sends a lightweight
.B POST /heartbeat
independently of the self-check cycle.
A 404 response triggers an immediate re-registration.
If unset, this timer uses the same interval as
.BR CHECK_SECONDS .
.PP
Sub-instances for registering in additional VAS servers can be managed
with
.BR vac-sub-instance (8)
and are supervised by
.BR vac-sub-manager (8).
.SH EXTRA FIELDS
Two dictionaries of arbitrary key-value pairs can be attached to each
registration:
.TP
.B extra_imperative
Changes to this dictionary bump the inventory version on
.BR vas (8),
causing all consumers to re-fetch.
Scripts placed in
.I /etc/vac/extras_imperative.d/
are executed each cycle; their JSON output is stored under the script's
basename (without extension) as the key.
.TP
.B extra_informative
Purely informational. Changes never bump the version.
Scripts are placed in
.IR /etc/vac/extras_informative.d/ .
.SH CONFIGURATION
.B vac
reads
.I /etc/vac/vac.conf
and overlays in
.IR /etc/vac/vac.conf.d/ .
Key variables:
.TP
.B VAS_HOST
Hostname or IP of the VAS server. The port defaults to
.B 8000
if omitted.
.TP
.B VAS_SCHEME
Protocol scheme:
.B http
(default) or
.BR https .
.TP
.B CHECK_SECONDS
Self-check interval in seconds (default:
.BR 300 ).
.TP
.B HEARTBEAT_SECONDS
Independent liveness interval (default: same as
.BR CHECK_SECONDS ).
.TP
.B SYNC_CLIENTS
If
.BR true ,
download the full inventory to
.I /var/lib/vac/clients.json
whenever a new version is detected (default:
.BR true ).
.TP
.B EXTRAS_ENABLED
Enable the extra-fields subsystem (default:
.BR false ).
.TP
.B PARALLEL_MODE
Controls sub-instance parallelism:
.B both
(default),
.BR only_parallel ,
or
.BR only_main .
.TP
.B LOG_LEVEL
Log verbosity:
.B no
|
.B normal
|
.B debug
(default:
.BR normal ).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/vac/vac.conf
Main configuration file.
.TP
.I /etc/vac/vac.conf.d/
Drop-in configuration overlays.
.TP
.I /etc/vac/vac-id
Persistent UUID assigned to this machine (mode 0600).
.TP
.I /etc/vac/extras_imperative.d/
Scripts producing imperative extra fields (JSON output, 10 s timeout).
.TP
.I /etc/vac/extras_informative.d/
Scripts producing informative extra fields.
.TP
.I /var/lib/vac/clients.json
Local copy of the network inventory (when
.BR SYNC_CLIENTS=true ).
.TP
.I /var/lib/vac/identity.json
The last confirmed registration data used for self-check comparisons.
.TP
.I /var/lib/vac/version
The inventory version last seen from VAS.
.TP
.I /usr/share/vac/vac.conf.defaults
Reference copy of all configuration variables with documentation.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vac-register (8),
.BR vac-sub (8),
.BR vac-sub-manager (8),
.BR vac-sub-instance (8),
.BR vas (8),
.BR val (8),
.BR systemctl (1)
